{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795430400,"nonce":"YLHyC0OQEtep4daNz5O01dd1VPA=","message":"Fixed in 939d7bd5dbfdc390065e9d46f4320fb2922a4603.\n\nBug: tick_scroll_physics passes the unclamped gap to tick_scrollbar's hide timer; RenderTree::scrollbar_wake_in gives the next fade deadline, and a parked desktop window wakes for it (frame_dirty + wake_at). iOS polls RenderTree::scrollbar_fade_due in needs_render. Web draws every rAF and Android wakes every 100 ms idle, so neither stalled.\n\nPerf: a scroll container whose scrollbar fades by itself (Auto/Hover) and that nothing above can move, with no overlay open, has its scrollbar left out of the batch and drawn each frame from the recorded screen transform and clip (held_scrollbars.rs), so its fade is not off-rows animation and the frame takes the fast path.\n\nEvidence: cn_demo window with the scripted swipe (BLINC_BENCH_WHEEL=.cn-calendar-months), motion trace: the page scrollbar now fades during the wait before the swipes, as fast-path frames; no full frame of the run is gated on scroll_gliding (it was 34-45 per run). Test a_fading_scrollbar_over_still_content_takes_the_fast_path: Rows path pixel-equal to the Full reference each step at 1x and 2x, and no full paint after the scroll; it fails with the hold switched off (step 0 differs by 1412 px). Unit tests in widgets/scroll/hide.rs for the timer.\n\nWhat is not done, filed as ace1a2f634a16e41579456c3464fd6c8e4c7c32b924dca75ca26be69615a5a9e: the fade still full-paints for a container under a moving or scrolling ancestor, or with an overlay open.","files":null}]}